<h2><span id=3D"Create_new_expression_functions_with_plugin_.28New_in_4.0.0=
_.29"></span><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Create_new_expression_functi=
ons_with_plugin_(New_in_4.0.0_)">Create new expression functions with plugi=
n <sup> (New in 4.0.0 )</sup></span></h2>
<p>If you need a new function that doesn't exist in core, you can create on=
e with a plugin. Such a new function is created using the  <a href=3D"https=
://www.limesurvey.org/manual/ExpressionManagerStart" title=3D"ExpressionMan=
agerStart">expressionManagerStart</a> event.
</p>
<h1><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"ExpressionScript_knows_which_variable=
s_are_local">ExpressionScript knows which variables are local</span></h1>
<p>In order to properly build the JavaScript for a page, EM needs to know w=
hich variables are set on the page, and what their JavaScript ID is (e.g., =
for document.getElementById(x)). It must also know which variables are set =
on other pages (so that it can ensure that the needed &lt;input type=3D'hid=
den' value=3D'x'&gt; fields are present and populated).
</p><p><br>
</p>
<h2><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Cascading_Conditions">Cascading Condi=
tions</span></h2>
